# codeloop lane: market (v1)

Run `codeloop card show <id>` first; the card says which stage it is in. Gates are approved only by a person.

| Stage | Skill | Output | Done check | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| brief | plan | marketing/{id}/brief.md | `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/brief.md --has 'audience:' 'claim:' 'metric:'` |  |
| draft | design | marketing/{id}/blog.md | `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/blog.md --has 'claim:'` | copy (owner, after the check passes) |
| publish | ship | marketing/{id}/published.md | `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/published.md --has 'url:'` | publish (owner, before the stage runs) |
| measure | reflect | marketing/{id}/result.md | `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/result.md --has 'verdict:'` |  |

## brief

1. Run `codeloop card show <id>`. It prints the output path, the done check, the stage notes and any earlier rejection notes. Follow those over anything remembered.
2. Run `codeloop wiki inject --files <files you expect to touch>` and read every page it prints.
3. Do the work with the `plan` skill (.claude/commands/plan.md). Plan a task — write spec to tasks/todo.md, enter plan mode
4. Write the result to `marketing/{id}/brief.md`.
5. Run `codeloop card advance <id>`. It runs `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/brief.md --has 'audience:' 'claim:' 'metric:'`. If it exits 2, read the output, fix the work and run it again. Stop after 3 failures: the card parks as stuck for the owner.

## draft

1. Run `codeloop card show <id>`. It prints the output path, the done check, the stage notes and any earlier rejection notes. Follow those over anything remembered.
2. Run `codeloop wiki inject --files <files you expect to touch>` and read every page it prints.
3. Do the work with the `design` skill (.claude/commands/design.md). Architecture before code — generate lightweight spec from codebase analysis
4. Write the result to `marketing/{id}/blog.md`.
5. Run `codeloop card advance <id>`. It runs `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/blog.md --has 'claim:'`. If it exits 2, read the output, fix the work and run it again. Stop after 3 failures: the card parks as stuck for the owner.
6. The card then waits at gate `copy` for the owner. Stop there. Never run `codeloop approve` yourself.

## publish

0. This stage changes something public. The card waits at gate `publish` as it enters. Do nothing until a person has approved it.
1. Run `codeloop card show <id>`. It prints the output path, the done check, the stage notes and any earlier rejection notes. Follow those over anything remembered.
2. Run `codeloop wiki inject --files <files you expect to touch>` and read every page it prints.
3. Do the work with the `ship` skill (.claude/commands/ship.md). Close the loop — QA, deploy staging, deploy prod, verify, close task
4. Write the result to `marketing/{id}/published.md`.
5. Run `codeloop card advance <id>`. It runs `codeloop check file marketing/{id}/published.md --has 'url:'`. If it exits 2, read the output, fix the work and run it again. Stop after 3 failures: the card parks as stuck for the owner.

